  abstract: "Effective step-by-step assembly instructions depend on visual design characteristics that reduce ambiguity and cognitive load, yet there is no clear consensus on which characteristics contribute to instructional effectiveness. This gap becomes pressing as recent advances in artificial intelligence have increased interest in automatically generating assembly instructions from engineering data and process descriptions. To scope what is already known, we conducted a systematic scoping review of existing research on effective visual assembly instructions. This paper presents our methods and findings, mapping the current state of research, highlighting remaining gaps, and calling for more systematic empirical studies. By scoping existing efforts, we provide a concrete starting point for future work on the visual design of assembly instructions."
  url: "https://mixality.de/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Blattgerste2026Assembly.pdf"
